*****************************************************************************
*
** Released by: Texas Instruments Inc.
* Part: TPS259830ONRGE (derived from TI model TPS259830LNRGE, Final 1.10)
* Date: 09OCT2023
* Model Type: TRANSIENT
* Simulator: PSPICE
* Simulator Version: 17.4-2019 S064
* EVM Order Number: NA
* EVM Users Guide: SLUUCW7
* Datasheet: SLVSHH5
*
* Model Version: Final 1.10
*
*****************************************************************************
*
* Updates:
*
* Derived circuit-breaker version (not a TI release):
*     1. Overcurrent response = circuit breaker (datasheet SLVSHH5C, 7.3.3.2):
*        IFT > IOUT > ILIM discharges ITIMER; after dV_ITIMER the FET is
*        turned off and an internal fault is latched (7.3.8). No active
*        current regulation. Latch-off / auto-retry via RETRY_DLY / NRETRY
*        as in the original model.
*        Implemented by hard-wiring TI's internal switch CB=1; the global
*        '.PARAM cb' was removed. Additional fixes for the CB path:
*        a) The internal output crowbar (S10, 0.01 mOhm OUT->GND) is disabled.
*           TI fired it on fast-trip/thermal/>60 A (and with CB=1 also on a CB
*           trip) while the FET was still on -> non-physical kA shoot-through
*           from IN (2.7 kA on CB trip, 8.4 kA on output short) and ngspice
*           convergence failures. The FET is switched off by the internal gate
*           pull-down; OUT then discharges through the load / short.
*        b) The CB fault is held until the FET has been off for 5 us and is
*           then released (CB latch reset), so the fault logic always sees a
*           clean fault pulse and latch-off / auto-retry (RETRY_DLY, NRETRY)
*           work.
*        c) The gate clamp diode D7 now has a 1 kOhm series resistor (was
*           ideal). Without the crowbar, D3/D7 otherwise short the output into
*           an ideal source at turn-off (ngspice "timestep too small").
*           Effect in normal operation: about 20 mV more gate voltage.
*        d) dVdT node: 10 pF internal capacitance and a softer clamp diode
*           D1 (N=1 instead of 0.1). Without them the node jumps from 23 V to
*           0 V at turn-off -> ngspice "timestep too small" (V_U2_V10).
*           Plus 10k load on the ideal source V_U2_V10 (its pA branch current
*           could not converge below the round-off noise of the power path).
*     2. ngspice robustness: both TABLE E-sources rewritten as VALUE{pwl()}
*        (same values, input clamped to table range). ngspice would otherwise
*        create XSPICE devices and set trtol=1 globally -> stalls with tiny
*        timesteps. Also '.OPTIONS XTRTOL=7 METHOD=GEAR' (GLOBAL!): ngspice maps
*        the VSWITCH switches to XSPICE as well (xtrtol), and trapezoidal
*        integration rings on the 1 ns logic RC stages and flips latches (gear).
*        NOTE: pwl() and xtrtol are ngspice syntax -> file is meant for
*        ngspice/KiCad, not PSpice.
*        Retry-counter expressions (E_U5_ABM1/2/4/6) use bounded divisions;
*        with NRETRY at GND TI's version produced ~1e7..1e15 V internal nodes.
*        ILIM threshold (246u*I*1460)/V(ILIM) was 0/0 at IOUT=0 (thermal
*        shutdown from current limit aborted); ILIM pin current now has a floor
*        at IOUT=10 mA (2.46 uA), so the threshold stays 1460/RILIM+0.11.
*        Comparators (COMP/COMPHYS_BASIC_GEN_CB) continuous (tanh, 10 uV) instead
*        of hard IF(); hard ones chattered on slow ramps (thermal timer).
*        Same for the threshold stage of INV/BUF_DELAY and ONE_SHOT_CB timing.
*        SR latches without clamp diodes: while S/R is active the latch node
*        is pulled linearly to VDD/VSS (10 ohm, tau 10 ns). TI's +-5 A against
*        N=0.1 diodes made latches flip under trap (no auto-retry).
*        RETRY_DLY idle sink fades out at 0 V (was pulling the pin to -39 mV,
*        making later retry delays 5 % longer -> only 3 instead of 4 retries).
*        FAULT_OK/THERMAL_OK are cleared by the retry pulse (otherwise RETRY_DLY
*        was not discharged at the next fault -> retries 2..n came too early).
*        Internal logic now uses the internal PG state instead of the voltage on
*        the open-drain PG pin (without a pull-up the model never left the
*        startup state: no ITIMER, no CB trip).
*     3. ONE_SHOT_CB rebuilt: TI's self-holding loop OUT->CH->OUT has two valid
*        solutions and ngspice fired spurious pulses (resetting latches). Now
*        the pulse state is stored on a capacitor (set by IN, reset when the
*        timing node is done); pulse width unchanged (T x 1 ns).
*
*     KiCad/ngspice usage:
*       - Simulator settings: compatibility mode 'PSpice' or 'LTspice and PSpice'
*         (needed for the VSWITCH switches and PARAMS: syntax).
*       - Subcircuit TPS259830ONRGE, pin order see .SUBCKT line below.
*       - The file sets METHOD=GEAR (do not override with trap).
*     Notes for simulation (ngspice):
*       - Set a maximum time step <= 5 us (KiCad: transient 'max step', or a
*         time step of 1 us). Several internal timing pulses are 0.5..1.5 us
*         wide; with a coarse automatic step they can be missed (late trip,
*         no retry). Validated with max step 0.5 / 1 / 2 / 5 us.
*       - Validated (VIN 10/13.2/14.6 V, RILIM 82 ohm, CITIMER 4.7 nF/open):
*         CB trip after ITIMER, transient blanking, latch-off, 4 retries with
*         RETRY_DLY/NRETRY open, infinite retries with CRETRY_DLY=220 pF,
*         output short (fast-trip), start into overload with current limit
*         and thermal shutdown + retries.
*       - TI's ~40 A / 10 ns blip on IIN at enable/retry (internal 100 nF VIN
*         sample cap recharged via the IN pin) removed: cap fed from an
*         internal copy of VIN.
*
*     4. All helper subcircuits and global models renamed with suffix '_CB'
*        so this file can be included together with the TI L model.
*
* Final 1.10
* The follwing features are modified as per the latest datasheet.
*     1. Current limit (ILIM)- Current at ILIM pin is made a function of IOUT.
*     2. Retry and Nretry functionality
*     3. dVdT functionality
*     4. Fast trip functionality
*
* Final 1.00
* Release to Web.
*
*****************************************************************************
*
* Model Usage Notes:
*
* A. Features have been modelled
*	1. Startup
*	2. Programmable Current Limit and Fast-trip
*	3. IMON Current Indicator Output 
*	4. Undervoltage Lockout
*	5. Overvoltage Lockout 
*	6. Programmable dV/dT Control
*	7. Power Good
*   8. Auto-retry and latch off functionality
*	9. Thermal Shutdown time vs Power Dissipation
*
* B. Features haven't been modelled
*	1. Input supply current vs Input voltage during Normal operation
*	2. Input supply current vs Input voltage at Shutdown
*	3. Temperature dependent characteristics are not modelled. Thermal Shutdown Time vs Power Dissipation
*      is modelled such that temperature is not taken into account and only Power dissipation vs time is taken.
*
*****************************************************************************

